{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review landlord taxation and mortgage interest relief to protect rental housing",
        "additional_details": "Small independent landlords provide essential rental homes, often investing personal savings and taking significant financial risks. Rising taxes, restricted mortgage interest relief and increasing costs may force some to sell, potentially reducing rental supply and increasing rents.\r\nWe support fair taxation and tenant protections but urge the Government to assess the cumulative impact and consider a proportionate system that protects responsible landlords, tenants and the rental housing market.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to conduct a comprehensive review of taxation affecting small independent landlords, including the property income tax increases from April 2027 and restrictions on mortgage interest relief, & consider a more proportionate system that would better protect rental housing supply.",
